I did most of PJR-F4MG, but it is not complete. The English versions of the starter kata set are not written, because PJR-BXYM (which decides that set) is still in progress. I also couldn't confirm that the docs site builds (`npm run docs:build`).

**What was made**
- **English Quick Start:** `docs/en/specdojo/guides/quick-start-guide.md` is a full translation of the Japanese guide and uses the same id. Links to other guides still lead to the Japanese pages, and their link text says "(Japanese)".
- **Entry pages and README:** `docs/en/index.md`, `docs/index.md` and the English section of `README.md` now point to the English Quick Start. They also say that Japanese is the source of truth.
- **Tracking which Japanese version was translated:** English pages now carry `specdojo.translated_from` in their frontmatter, holding the source language and the commit. The field is optional and was added to `docs/specdojo/schemas/v1/common-frontmatter.schema.yaml`. The rule is written in the ID standard (`id-and-file-naming-standard.md`). I also added `docs/en/specdojo/guides/**/*.md` to the frontmatter checks in `.remarkrc.yaml`.
- **Ticket:** the work table, the results and a "CHANGELOG に書く事項" subsection with draft lines are filled in. `CHANGELOG.md` was not changed.

**Language decisions (recorded in the ticket)**
- English kata go in `docs/en/specdojo/{rulebooks,recipes,samples,templates}/`, with the same file names and ids as the Japanese ones. The repo already lists `ja` and `en` as locales, so no new ids or link rewrites are needed.
- The setting is `kata_locale` at the top level of `.specdojo/specdojo.config.json` (`ja` or `en`, default `ja`). If an English version is missing, the Japanese one is used.
- `init` asks `Kata language (ja / en) [ja]:`; without prompts it is `--kata-locale`.
- `kata list` gets a `LOCALE` column at the end, so existing columns keep their positions. It shows `ja (fallback)` when no English version exists.
- These are decisions only; none of this is implemented yet.

**Still open (marked `_UNDECIDED_` in the ticket)**
- Whether the `init` default should follow the OS language.
- Whether the orchestrator and CLI messages should switch language with the same setting.
- The contents of the starter kata set (waiting for PJR-BXYM).

**Checks**
- Prettier and `npm run validate:history-links` passed.
- I did not run `npm run docs:build`, because it rewrites `.specdojo/doc-index.json`, which I'm not allowed to write.
- The other lint and schema checks run in the parent runner after this step.

